  "body": "Tucked well away from the main road down a private driveway, this 170sqm (approx) home sits on a rare 1,286sqm freehold site. Offering plenty of space for growing families to stretch out, it combines immediate comfort with long-term land banking or potential development upside under Mixed Housing Suburban zoning. With motivated owners ready for their next step, this is a smart, flexible acquisition in a prime coastal pocket.\r\n\r\nWhat You’ll Love:\r\n- Dual sun-drenched decks flanking either side of the generous main living lounge to capture all-day light\r\n- Open-plan dining and practical kitchen hub connecting directly out to outdoor entertaining space\r\n- All four bedrooms positioned conveniently on the same level, which families usually prefer\r\n- Full family bathroom on the main level plus a dedicated lower-level laundry room\r\n- Massive lower-level footprint featuring a double garage, workshop, and expansive under-house storage\r\n- Sunny lawn areas with heaps of room for kids and pets to safely play\r\n- On-site wastewater and stormwater infrastructure on a private 1,286sqm freehold site\r\n\r\nBest Bits From the Vendor:\r\n\"Living here is so peaceful and quiet... because you're set back off the road, there's minimal road noise, and you honestly forget anyone else is around. On a clear night, you can see millions of stars because there are no street lights right over us, it was actually the perfect spot for watching an eclipse! In the day, the way the sun hits the lounge makes it so cosy, and we love just sitting there listening to the birds cheeping, watching the Tui's darting through the trees, and the fantails fluttering about outside. It's just been a really comfortable place to live.\"\r\n\r\nLifestyle & Location:\r\nPositioned off Cranston Street, this pocket of Torbay flies under the radar while keeping you connected to everything the North Shore coastal lifestyle offers. You are a short drive or easy walk to local school zones, Torbay Village cafes, and local shops. On weekends, the family can head straight down to Waiake Beach or Long Bay Regional Park for coastal walks and swims, enjoying an established, quiet community setting.\r\n\r\nWhether you are searching for an honest family home with room to grow, or looking to secure a prime piece of land with on-site services ready to explore, 21 Cranston Street presents a clear opportunity. \r\n\r\nWatch 'The Reel Open Home' - https://youtube.com/shorts/Wzu1B1Y2wKg\r\n\r\n*Floor area and land area sourced from Auckland Council records.\r\nAgents happy to work in with your buyers.",
